The issues for determination referred to a Five Judge Bench of the Supreme Court, were as follows;
"5........................................................................
 5.1.

For ease of comprehension Section 5A(1) and Sections 17(1) and 17(4) of the Act of 1894 are extracted below;
 "5A. Hearing of objec  
person interested in any land which has been notified under section 4, sub-section (1), as being needed or likely to be needed for a public purpose or for a company may, within thirty days from the date of the publication of the notification, object to the acquisition of the land or of any land in the locality, as the case may be."

(xi) That, having been said necessary reference is made to Section 114 of the Act of 2013 which reads as follows;
"114. Repeal and saving.(1) The Land Acquisition Act, 1894 (1 of 1894) is hereby repealed.
(2) Save as otherwise provided in this Act the repeal under sub-section (1) shall not be held to prejudice or affect the general application of section 6 of the General Clauses Act, 1897 (10 of 1897) with regard to the effect of repeals."

(ii) In The Fruit & Vegetable Merchants Union vs. The Delhi Improvement Trust , the Supreme Court considered the term "vest"
and observed as follows;
"(11) .....

